meta {
  name: Cancel Household Policy
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/households/{{policyCancelHouseholdId}}/policies/{{policyCancelPolicyId}}/cancel
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "sold"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("the policy is off the books", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.policyStatus).to.equal("Cancelled");
    expect(body.active).to.equal(false);
  });

  test("and says why", function () {
    const cancellation = res.getBody().cancellation;
    expect(cancellation.reason).to.equal("sold");
    // Dropped for a named reason — only `other` carries free text.
    expect(cancellation.note).to.equal(null);
    expect(cancellation.cancelledAt).to.be.a("string");
  });

  test("never echoes internals", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("branchId");
    expect(body.cancellation).to.not.have.property("cancelledBy");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /households/:id/policies/:policyId/cancel

  Cancel one of the household's policies **and record why** — the policy card's
  **Cancel policy** button.

  - **Module:** `clients` OR `crm_service`
  - **Permission:** `clients:write` **OR** `crm_service:write` (same gate as
    **Update Household Policy** — the service team holds `crm_service:write` and
    nothing on the Sold side)
  - **Data scope:** `own` collapses to **branch**; the household in the path is
    the authorisation, so a policy that is not this household's is a **404**

  ## Why this is not `status: "Cancelled"` on the PATCH
  A cancellation carries a fact a field patch has nowhere to put — the reason.
  `Cancelled` is therefore a **flow-only** status now, like `Cancel Rewrite` and
  `Company Transfer`: **Update Household Policy** and the Sold card's
  `PATCH /policies/:id` both refuse to *set* it (400), and this endpoint is its
  only writer on the edit paths. Re-sending `Cancelled` to a policy that already
  holds it is accepted as a no-op, so a cancelled policy stays editable.

  ## Body
  | Field | Type | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `reason` | `"sold" \| "changed_carrier" \| "other"` | required |
  | `note` | string ≤ 500, nullable | **required for `other`** (blank after trimming is a 400); **dropped** for the named reasons |

  No date — the cancellation is stamped with server time.

  ## What it does
  - `policyStatus` → `Cancelled`, `active` → `false` (so it stops counting
    towards the household and stops being scheduled for renewal calls)
  - stores `cancellation: { reason, note, cancelledAt, cancelledBy }`
  - recounts the household's stored `totalActivePolicies` (the Clients list
    sorts on it)
  - writes a **"Policy cancelled"** edit-log row (status and cancellation
    reason), readable with `agency:changelogs:read`

  Nothing touches the Sold pipeline, a lead or a chargeback — use **Cancel &
  rewrite** / **Company transfer** for a replacement.

  Reinstating (**Update Household Policy** with `status: "Active"`) clears the
  stored reason.

  ## Response
  The saved **`PolicySummary`**, with `cancellation: { reason, note,
  cancelledAt }` (`cancelledBy` stays server-side). `cancellation` is `null` on
  every policy not cancelled through this endpoint, including migrated ones that
  read `Cancelled`.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | Unknown `reason`; `other` without a `note`; `note` over 500 characters |
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | Both `clients` and `crm_service` disabled, or the caller holds neither write |
  | 404 | Policy or household outside the caller's scope, or the policy is not this household's |
  | 409 | The policy is already off the books — Cancelled, Lapsed, retired into a replacement, or otherwise inactive and not Pending |
}
